      "writtenOn": "2012-11-17T16:14:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to get in the habit of having a single try/except block per function.  This one is easier to read like this:\ntry:\n    session \u003d self.get_session()\n    ref \u003d session.query(PolicyModel).filter_by(id\u003dpolicy_id).one()\n    return ref.to_dict()\nexcept sqlalchemy.orm.exc.NoResultFound:\n    raise exception.PolicyNotFound(policy_id\u003dpolicy_id)\n\n\nIt has the added benefit that, if we discover additional exceptions we need to deal with, they are only new except blocks, not re ordering the whole method.",
      "revId": "bbd218761e841eabc7560485574aa5944741219c",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
